ages\\/1940265708878807040\\/BH0a5ReE.jpg","name":"Final Cut Tile \\ud83c\\uddfa\\ud83c\\uddf8","screen_name":"FinalCutTile","verified":false,"is_blue_verified":true},"grok_user":{"id_str":"1720665183188922368","profile_image_url_https":"https:\\/\\/pbs.twimg.com\\/profile_images\\/1893219113717342208\\/Vgg2hEPa.jpg","name":"Grok","screen_name":"grok","highlighted_label":{"description":"xAI","badge":{"url":"https:\\/\\/pbs.twimg.com\\/profile_images\\/1769430779845611520\\/lIgjSJGU_bigger.jpg"},"url":{"urlType":"DeepLink","url":"https:\\/\\/twitter.com\\/xai"},"userLabelType":"BusinessLabel","userLabelDisplayType":"Badge"},"verified":false,"is_blue_verified":true,"verified_type":"Business"},"id":"isjb6FvZ1efGdlhboC7YGXdrd","conversation_preview":[{"message":"If the president pardons someone, does that protect them from being tried under UCMJ?","sender":"USER","grokMode":"NORMAL","mediaUrls":[]},{"message":"No, a presidential pardon does not extend to protect an individual from being tried under the Uniform Code of Military Justice (UCMJ). Here\'s why:\\nJurisdiction: The UCMJ applies to members of the military, and it is a separate legal system from civilian federal law where a presidential pardon would apply. The authority of the President to pardon under Article II, Section 2 of the U.S. Constitution generally pertains to offenses against the United States, which are typically federal civilian crimes.\\nMilitary Law: The UCMJ is administered by military courts, and while the President is the Commander in Chief, the military judicial system has its own processes. A pardon by the President might affect federal civilian prosecutions but does not directly influence military court proceedings unless explicitly stated otherwise.\\nHistorical Precedent: There have been instances where individuals pardoned by the President for federal crimes have still faced military justice. For example, in the case of U.S. v. Loving (1987), the Supreme Court upheld a UCMJ conviction despite a presidential pardon for related civilian offenses.\\nSpecific Language: In rare cases, if a presidential pardon explicitly mentions protection from military prosecution, it could potentially affect UCMJ proceedings. However, such specificity in pardons is not common.\\nTherefore, if an individual is subject to military law, a presidential pardon for civilian offenses does not inherently shield them from military prosecution under the UCMJ. However, the specifics of each case, including the language of the pardon and the nature of the charges under both systems, could influence outcomes in unique ways.","sender":"AGENT","grokMode":"NORMAL","mediaUrls":[]}],"destination":"destination_1","allowed_actions":["ASK_IT_YOURSELF"],"metadata":{"text":"Answer by Grok"}}}},"destination_objects":{"destination_1":{"type":"browser","data":{"url_data":{"url":"https:\\/\\/x.com\\/i\\/grok\\/share\\/isjb6FvZ1efGdlhboC7YGXdrd","vanity":"Grok"}}}},"components":["details_1"]}', 'type': 'STRING'}}, {'key': 'card_url', 'value': {'scribe_key': 'card_url', 'string_value': 'https://t.co/uiVfhPYHEl', 'type': 'STRING'}}], 'card_platform': {'platform': {'audience': {'name': 'production'}, 'device': {'name': 'Swift', 'version': '12'}}}, 'name': 'unified_card', 'url': 'https://t.co/uiVfhPYHEl', 'user_refs_results': []}}, 'unmention_data': {}, 'edit_control': {'edit_tweet_ids': ['1881371432124580223'], 'editable_until_msecs': '1737392478000', 'is_edit_eligible': False, 'edits_remaining': '5'}, 'is_translatable': False, 'views': {'count': '2434', 'state': 'EnabledWithCount'}, 'source': '<a href="http://twitter.com/download/android" rel="nofollow">Twitter for Android</a>', 'legacy': {'bookmark_count': 2, 'bookmarked': False, 'created_at': 'Mon Jan 20 16:01:18 +0000 2025', 'conversation_id_str': '1881371432124580223', 'display_text_range': [0, 178], 'entities': {'hashtags': [], 'symbols': [], 'timestamps': [], 'urls': [{'display_url': 'x.com/i/grok/share/i…', 'expanded_url': 'https://x.com/i/g